    "title": "<p>Criteria for assigning primary site in extrauterine high-grade serous carcinoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "C. Blake Gilks",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 456.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Primary site</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"487\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Criteria for diagnosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Fallopian tube</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"487\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">STIC present</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; or</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mucosal HGSC present</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; or</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Part or entire length of tube inseparable from tubo-ovarian mass</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Ovary</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"487\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Both fallopian tubes separate from ovarian mass</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No STIC or mucosal HGSC in either tube<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tubo-ovarian<sup>b</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"487\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Fallopian tubes and ovaries not available for complete examination<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pathological findings consistent with extrauterine HGSC</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Peritoneal</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"487\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Both tubes and both ovaries fully examined</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No gross or microscopic evidence of STIC or HGSC in tubes<sup>a</sup> or ovaries</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">HGSC, high-grade serous carcinoma; STIC, serous tubal intraepithelial carcinoma.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Grossly normal fallopian tubes have been examined using the SEE-FIM (sectioning and extensively examining the fimbriated end) protocol to exclude microscopic disease.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>b</sup>This applies in small biopsy samples or HGSC developing after previous salpingo-oophorectomy with incomplete tubal examination, and it may apply in postchemotherapy surgical specimens.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
